{%- macro remediation(ctx, level) -%}
## 4. Remediation Recommendations

{% if ctx.actionable() | length == 0 %}
No remediation actions are required beyond routine patching and monitoring.
{% elif level == 'executive' %}
Recommended strategic priorities, in order:

{% if ctx.counts.get('critical') or ctx.counts.get('high') %}
1. **Stop the bleeding (0–30 days).** Remediate all critical and high findings;
   {{ (ctx.counts.get('critical',0) + ctx.counts.get('high',0)) }} item(s). These
   are the issues an attacker would use first.
{% endif %}
2. **Reduce attack surface (30–90 days).** Address medium findings
   ({{ ctx.counts.get('medium',0) }} item(s)) and remove exposed services that
   are not business-critical.
3. **Harden and verify (90–180 days).** Close low-severity hygiene gaps, then
   commission a focused retest to confirm closure.
4. **Sustain.** Fold recurring checks (TLS config, security headers, exposed
   admin interfaces, patch currency) into a quarterly cadence.

Indicative timelines assume normal change-management capacity; critical items
should be expedited.
{% elif level == 'remediation' %}
Prioritised action plan. Suggested SLA is measured from report delivery.

| # | Action | Risk | CVSS | Asset(s) | Effort | Suggested SLA | Owner |
|---|--------|------|------|----------|--------|---------------|-------|
{% for f in ctx.actionable() %}| {{ loop.index }} | {{ f.remediation | truncate(160) or f.title }} | {{ f.severity.value|upper }} | {{ '%.1f'|format(f.cvss_score) if f.cvss_score else '—' }} | `{{ f.target }}` | {{ ctx.effort(f) }} | {% set d = ctx.sla_days(f.severity.value) %}{{ (d ~ ' days') if d else 'best effort' }} | _assign_ |
{% endfor %}

**Verification.** Re-run the originating tool against each asset after the fix
(`ronin run <tool> --engagement {{ ctx.engagement.slug }} --target <asset>`), or
commission a retest. A finding is closed only when the check no longer fires.
{% else %}
Per-finding remediation. Items are ordered by severity.

